	1. Programming vs Coding
		a. Coding 
			i. Coding is the act of translating instructions into a programming language
		b. Programming 
			i. End-to-end process of creating software. It includes planning, designing, coding, testing, debugging, deploying, and maintaining applications.
	2. Python app 
		a. The “Python app” from the Python website is basically the Python interpreter + standard tools packaged for your operating system.
			i. It’s a programming runtime/environment used to build and run Python programs.
	3. REPL - Read–eval–print loop (REPL)
		a. Often referred to as "consoles", "terminals", or "prompts"
		b. Also termed an interactive top level or language shell, is a simple interactive computer programming environment that takes single user inputs, executes them, and returns the result to the user.
	4. Windows PowerShell
		a. Windows PowerShell is a command-line tool and scripting language built into Windows. (More powerful version of Command Prompt.)
		b. Instead of clicking through apps, you can type commands to:
		c. navigate folders, run programs (like Python scripts), manage files, automate, repetitive tasks
	5. Application Programming Interface (API)
		a. Think a middleman that allows different software applications to talk to each other
	6. Microsoft Azure
		a. Microsoft's Cloud computing platform
			i. Run virtual machines (servers)
			ii. Host websites and APIs
			iii. Store files and databases
			iv. Build apps, AI, and analytics solutions
			v. Set up networking, security, backup, and disaster recovery
		b. Best for scale/performance: Oracle → ADLS/Synapse → Power BI Import (incremental refresh)
		
		
	
